  "prefLabel": "Env-A 4602.39 Eligible biomass",
  "priorExpiration": "2009-03-30",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 4602.39 “Eligible biomass” means sustainably-harvested woody and herbaceous fuel sources that are available on a renewable or recurring basis, excluding old-growth timber, including dedicated energy crops and trees, agricultural food and feed crop residues, aquatic plants, unadulterated wood and wood residues, animal wastes, biogas, eligible liquid biofuels, and other clean organic wastes not mixed with other solid wastes. Eligible biomass includes biomass combusted at Schiller Station, as permitted effective March 7, 2006.\n\nSource. #9283, INTERIM, eff 10-1-08, EXPIRED: 3-30-09\n\nNew. #9444, eff 4-3-09; ss by #10468, eff 1-1-14 (from Env-A 4602.37); ss by #12967, eff 1-1-20 (from Env-A 4602.40)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a4600.html"
